        "original_id": "0b4dcfa8-6548-5792-b833-d14da3671c04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maria Brontë, Patrick Brontë, Elizabeth Brontë, Maria Branwell\n- Organizations: Cowan Bridge School\n- Topics: Brontë family, tuberculosis, typhoid outbreak\n\nFacts:\n- Patrick Brontë was born on 17 March 1777 and was an Irish priest and author who spent most of his adult life in England.\n- Maria Brontë, née Maria Branwell, was the mother of Maria Brontë.\n- Maria Brontë was born on 23 April 1814 and was the eldest daughter of Patrick Brontë and Maria Brontë, née Maria Branwell.\n- At Cowan Bridge School, a typhoid outbreak was followed by the deaths of the sisters Maria and Elizabeth from tuberculosis.\n- Maria Brontë died on 6 May 1825.\n- Patrick Brontë died on 7 June 1861.",
